# BrainRouter server — environment template
#
# Copy to `brainrouter/.env` (monorepo dev) or `~/.config/brainrouter/server.env`.
# Loaded automatically when the server starts.
#
# AI PROVIDERS (LLM / embeddings / reranker) are configured in the DATABASE via
# the dashboard (AI Providers) or POST /api/admin/providers — NOT here (ADR-012).
# The embedding VECTOR WIDTH is DB-driven too (derived from the embedder), so it
# is no longer set here. This file is only infra + a few operational knobs.
#
# Full knob reference: brainrouter-docs/configuration.md


# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres + pgvector connection (`DATABASE_URL` is also accepted). SQLite was
# removed (ADR-007) — the engine will not start without this. A local pgvector
# lives in deploy/postgres/.
BRAINROUTER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/brainrouter

# AES-256-GCM key that encrypts stored provider/integration API keys at rest.
# REQUIRED to save any secret via the dashboard. Generate: openssl rand -base64 32.
# BRAINROUTER_SECRET_KEY=


# ── Server auth (HTTP transport + dashboard; stdio ignores these) ─────────────
# BRAINROUTER_JWT_SECRET=            # 32-byte hex; REQUIRED in production (else sessions reset every boot)
# BRAINROUTER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=        # set once on first boot to seed the admin, then clear (the API key prints once)
# BRAINROUTER_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# BRAINROUTER_CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000   # prod dashboard origin(s), comma-separated (dev allows any localhost)
# BRAINROUTER_SYSTEM_ORG_ID=         # which org's DB providers back the brain's own calls (default: the seeded admin's org)
# The externally-reachable base URL of THIS server (scheme + host, no trailing slash).
# Drives the public meeting share links (`<PUBLIC_URL>/m/<token>`) AND the connector
# OAuth callback URL — one domain for both. Unset ⇒ share links are host-less (broken)
# and web-OAuth callbacks can't be built. Set it to your deployed domain in production.
# BRAINROUTER_PUBLIC_URL=https://app.yourdomain.com   # dev: http://localhost:3747


# ── Common tuning (optional; sensible defaults) ───────────────────────────────
# BRAINROUTER_LLM_MAX_CONCURRENT=2         # in-flight LLM cap — 1 for single-GPU LM Studio, 10+ for cloud
# BRAINROUTER_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=              # bound LLM calls (default: none — wait for the server)
# BRAINROUTER_JOB_RUNNER=on                # in-process job runner (extraction/graph/focus). Off = delegate to a worker service.
# BRAINROUTER_METRICS=on                   # expose GET /metrics (Prometheus). Default off → 404.


# ── Cache (optional; makes reads faster) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Redis-backed read cache for hot, global data (the CVE catalog, hot dashboard
# GETs). Purely an accelerator — with it UNSET the brain uses an in-process
# cache and everything still works; set it to share the cache across replicas
# and survive restarts. Requires the optional `ioredis` package (installed in
# the Docker image). Compose wires this automatically to the bundled redis.
# BRAINROUTER_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379   # or REDIS_URL


# ── Vulnerability intelligence (optional; enabled by default) ─────────────────
# NVD_API_KEY=                             # recommended for higher NVD rate limits; never exposed to clients
# BRAINROUTER_VULNERABILITY_SYNC=on        # scheduled NVD + CISA KEV + FIRST EPSS refresh and watch re-evaluation
# BRAINROUTER_VULNERABILITY_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS=900000          # normal refresh eligibility (15 min)
# BRAINROUTER_VULNERABILITY_PARTIAL_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS=60000   # resume an unfinished NVD page window promptly


# ── Pentest sandbox (optional; the pentest lens is OFF until these are set) ────
# The pentest lens NEVER runs on the host — every command runs in a throwaway,
# read-only, capability-dropped Docker container routed through an intercepting
# proxy. Supply the two images + the proxy address (images are never auto-pulled).
# Full setup: deploy/pentest/README.md.
# BRAINROUTER_PENTEST_IMAGE=brainrouter-pentest:local        # build: docker build -f deploy/pentest/Dockerfile -t brainrouter-pentest:local .
# BRAINROUTER_PENTEST_PROXY_IMAGE=mitmproxy/mitmproxy:11.1.3 # docker pull it first
# BRAINROUTER_PENTEST_PROXY_URL=http://proxy:8080            # egress the sandbox routes through
# BRAINROUTER_PENTEST_PROXY_API=http://proxy:8081            # proxy control API (request-history tools)
# BRAINROUTER_PENTEST_PROXY_TOKEN=                           # optional bearer for the proxy API


# Everything else — pgvector index tuning, distillation triggers, sweepers,
# skill pre-warming, rate limits, per-task model overrides, PostgreSQL HNSW
# params, etc. — is documented in brainrouter-docs/configuration.md. Set those
# there only when you need them.
